WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:04.480
If Impractical Jokers isn't your thing, Impractical
Jokers: The Movie isn't going to change your

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:05.000
mind.

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:08.560
If you dig the show's ridiculous sense of
humor, though, you'll like the movie, too.

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:11.240
No, it's not perfect but then again, what
is?

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:16.180
Unsurprisingly, the best thing about Impractical
Jokers: The Movie is also the best thing about

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:19.780
Impractical Jokers the television show: It
has a setup that works.

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:23.000
The movie's heart is the hidden-camera pranks,
just like the series.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.300
Typically, these all use the same format.

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:29.900
Members of the cast are put into fairly mundane
situations for example, they need to flag

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:33.700
down help when their car breaks down on the
highway while their comrades watch from afar.

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:38.020
The Joker or Jokers in the hot seat are wearing
earpieces, and have to do whatever the others

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:38.580
tell them.

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:41.640
If you've seen the show, you know exactly
what to expect.

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:44.760
"Joe, just open-mouth sneeze on the wall."

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:52.460
If a Joker refuses to follow directions or
can't accomplish his goal, he gets a thumbs

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:53.000
down.

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:55.860
Whoever has the most thumbs-downs at the end
loses.

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:57.860
The movie works the same way.

00:00:57.860 --> 00:00:58.520
It's just longer.

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:03.940
Sal, Q, Joe, and Murr are all extremely talented
improvisers, and easily come up with new ways

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:07.920
to torture their friends and spin their team
members' outrageous demands into comedy gold.

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:09.220
So what if we've seen it before?

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:11.420
Like they say, if it's not broken, don't fix
it.

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:15.460
"Yeah that's solid, that's good.

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:16.640
That's a for-suresky."

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:21.240
At this point, there are over 200 episodes
of the show, plus more than 30 TV specials.

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:25.620
That's a lot of Impractical Jokers, and while
the movie doesn't reference it all, it does

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:26.380
the best it can.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:29.720
One gag plays on Sal's well-established fear
of cats.

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:33.900
Another recalls a bit from all the way back
in season two when Q had to teach his parents

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:34.440
sex ed.

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:38.300
If you've seen every episode of Impractical
Jokers, these callbacks should delight you.

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:40.860
"Oh, God that looks like it's, it was…"

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:46.600
"Oh, it's meowing"

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:50.200
On the other hand, if you're new to the show,
your mileage will probably vary.

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:54.160
The movie catches newbies up on what they
need to know, but a few punchlines don't really

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:56.420
land unless you've been following the gang
the whole time.

00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:59.920
Impractical Jokers is a funny show, but it's
a modest one.

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:03.000
A lot of the action takes place in shopping
malls and city parks.

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:06.880
The challenges are simple, and on average
the punishments are pretty low key.

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:11.060
"Three, two, one, shhh..."

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:16.600
Not so in the movie.

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:20.560
While the film still relies on the charm and
talent of its cast for its humor, the bigger

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:23.240
budget and extra scope gives the group room
to go a little bit bigger.

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:26.980
It's hard to imagine Jaden Smith stopping
by to help with one of the pranks in the show.

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:32.140
The guys could've easily made a bigger, more
extravagant episode of the TV series and called

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:32.840
it a movie.

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:35.620
Instead, they decided to give the film an
actual story.

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:36.800
It's not clear why.

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:40.940
The film opens when the Jokers were still
in high school, and chronicles their mishaps

00:02:40.940 --> 00:02:42.700
at a Paula Abdul concert gone wrong.

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:47.520
In the present day, the quartet get the opportunity
to redeem themselves when Abdul recognizes

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:50.820
them at a Red Lobster and invites them to
a party she's throwing in Miami.

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:52.430
There's just one problem:

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:54.260
"She sent three tickets!"

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:57.840
And so, as the Jokers travel from Long Island
to Florida, they compete in a series of prank

00:02:57.940 --> 00:02:59.440
battles to see who gets left out.

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:03.420
Unfortunately, the pre-scripted plot scenes
drag everything to a halt.

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:08.540
Joe, Q, Sal, and Murr are funny guys, but
they're not great actors and none of the jokes

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:12.760
really hit there's a reason their sketch comedy
spinoff didn't even finish its six-episode

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:13.460
run, after all.

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:17.300
Impractical Jokers doesn't need to explain
why these guys are playing pranks.

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:18.140
It's just what they do.

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:21.180
Even worse, the story doesn't really lead
to anything, either.

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:23.960
It's mostly there to fill time, and it feels
completely unnecessary.

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:31.660
"What advice would you give filmmakers starting
out in order to help them to avoid the pitfalls

00:03:31.660 --> 00:03:32.640
that you clearly fell into."

00:03:34.220 --> 00:03:37.180
Impractical Jokers is uncomfortable, but it's
never cruel.

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:41.180
While Jackass is about inflicting pain and
Borat goes out of its way to make its targets

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:45.280
look like idiots, Impractical Jokers' only
real victims are the Jokers themselves.

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:50.560
Regular civilians might suffer minor inconveniences,
but the final joke is always on Joe, Sal,

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:51.260
Murr, and Q.

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:55.420
In the movie, the Jokers often decide it's
better to lose a challenge than put unsuspecting

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:57.100
civilians in awkward situations.

00:03:57.420 --> 00:04:01.000
Instead of robbing Impractical Jokers of its
edge, the compassionate approach actually

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:02.080
makes the movie funnier.

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:05.300
Impractical Jokers isn't just a prank show.

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:06.000
It's a competition.

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:09.880
While the ultimate goal might be making the
audience laugh, each member of the cast spends

00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:12.340
every episode doing his best to win the challenge
at hand.

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:16.400
After all, if you fail, you'll get turned
into a human pinata, forced to face down a

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:18.580
crowd of angry Bingo players, or worse.

00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:22.320
"When I tell you to you're gonna take a deep
breath, alright?

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:23.660
And… deep breath.”

00:04:23.669 --> 00:04:24.669
“Motherf----"

00:04:24.669 --> 00:04:25.979
Those punishments were all real.

00:04:25.979 --> 00:04:27.770
The one in the Movie isn't.

00:04:27.770 --> 00:04:31.330
Missing out on a fake party isn't exactly
the same as being strapped to a table while

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:34.200
tarantulas walk all over you, and the film
suffers for it.

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:37.220
The consequences aren't real, so there's no
reason to care.

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:40.960
The movie has "punishments," of course, and
they're some of the best parts of the film,

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:42.880
but they don't work the same way they do on
the show.

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:46.100
On TV, the punishments are consequences for
failure.

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:50.539
In the movie, they're random asides that pop
up as the Jokers travel across the country.

00:04:50.539 --> 00:04:54.280
That doesn't make them any less funny, but
it does make the movie even less exciting

00:04:54.280 --> 00:04:55.500
than an episode of television.

00:04:56.580 --> 00:05:01.160
Joe, Q, Sal, and Murr literally grew up together,
and their close bond comes through onscreen.

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:04.220
They know exactly how to push each other's'
buttons a skill that comes in pretty handy

00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:06.240
when you're trying to put your buddy through
hell.

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:09.640
But they have an easy camaraderie that lends
itself well to comedy.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:13.500
In a way, that's what makes Impractical Jokers'
pre-scripted scenes so jarring.

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:17.740
One of the things that makes Impractical Jokers
special is that the Jokers are clearly real

00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:18.260
people.

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:22.120
The film's story segments, however, transform
all of them into cartoon characters.

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:23.860
That really doesn't work.

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:27.120
The movie is at its best when their real-life
bond is on full display.

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:30.440
Impractical Jokers is a short movie.

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:33.939
It clocks in at just over an hour and a half,
and most of it breezes right by.

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:36.240
Near the end of the film, however, things
begin to drag.

00:05:36.820 --> 00:05:39.460
You're waiting for one big, final laugh that
never comes.

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:42.940
"Hell naw, to the naw naw naw.

00:05:45.380 --> 00:05:46.040
I'm so sorry."

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:48.240
Again, it's not that big of a deal.

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:50.990
The rest of the movie is fun and likable,
and you'll leave the theater having had a

00:05:50.990 --> 00:05:51.540
good time.

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:55.600
Still, something as good as Impractical Jokers:
The Movie deserves a real climax.

00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:57.600
Or at least a little broccoli time.

